From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:27:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] schema validation: reduce contention and allocation
 overhead

Keep application writes that fail a pending schema independent of validation
progress updates. Leave inactive attempt cleanup to bounded worker transactions,
fence initialization and checkpoints on the owning schema, and preserve staged
attempts under active schemas. Bound historical schema deletion and retain
SQLite-backed regressions for both commit orders and schema replacement.

Borrow document object validators instead of cloning the root union per document.
Share value traversal between ordinary diagnostics and union alternatives whose
errors are discarded, constructing diagnostic clones and context paths only when
they will be returned. Preserve acceptance, alternative order, root system-field
filtering, singleton errors, and final union diagnostics.

Keep the schema worker, lifecycle, attempt ownership, and SQLite test dependency
in one independently adoptable patch before optional Wasm execution. Document the
adoption boundary and include validator regressions and an ignored benchmark for
comparing the same fixtures before and after the allocation optimization.
